-- title:
--   An extra level at ℓ from a full level-m structure
-- statement:
--   Let $q,q'$ be primes and $a,b\in\mathbb{Q}$ be such that $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$ satisfies `IsIndefiniteRamifiedExactlyAt`: $0<a$ or $0<b$, and for a height-one prime $v$ of the integers of $\mathbb{Q}$ every nonzero element of $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}\mathbb{Q}_v$ is a unit exactly when $v$ contains $q$ or $q'$. Let $\Lambda$ be a $\mathbb{Z}$-submodule of $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$ that is an order maximal among orders for inclusion, let $N,m\in\mathbb{N}$, let $\ell$ be a prime dividing $m$, and let $L_0\subseteq\Lambda$ be a $\mathbb{Z}$-submodule with $\ell x\in L_0$ for all $x\in\Lambda$, closed under left multiplication by $\Lambda$, and of relative index $\ell^2$ in $\Lambda$ as additive subgroups. Let $S$ be a commutative ring in which $m$ is a unit, let $E$ be a fake elliptic curve over $S$ for $\Lambda$ and $N$ (a scheme $A$ over $\operatorname{Spec}S$ with relative group law $E.L$, two-dimensional fibres, a $\Lambda$-action `E.act` by morphisms over $S$, and the remaining data of the structure), and let $P$ be a full level-$m$ structure on $E$: a section $P.P$ over $\operatorname{Spec}S$ killed by $m$, whose $\Lambda$-orbit at each geometric point exhausts the $m$-torsion, and whose annihilator in $\Lambda$ is exactly $m\Lambda$. Assume that for every algebraically closed field $k$, every ring homomorphism $sk:S\to k$ and every $x\in\Lambda$ lying in $L_0$, if the point $x\cdot\big((m/\ell)\,P_{\bar{s}}\big)$ — the image under `E.act x` of the $(m/\ell)$-fold multiple of the specialisation of $P.P$ at the geometric point $\operatorname{Spec}k\to\operatorname{Spec}S$ — factors through `E.lev`, then it is the identity section. Then there is an `ExtraLevel` $K$ for $E$ at $\ell$ (a scheme with a closed immersion $K\to A$ whose sections form a $\Lambda$-stable subgroup killed by $\ell$, meeting `E.lev` only in the identity, with $K\to\operatorname{Spec}S$ finite, flat, locally of finite presentation of fibre rank $\ell^2$, and geometric fibres isomorphic to $(\mathbb{Z}/\ell)^2$ as groups) such that for every algebraically closed field $k$, every $sk:S\to k$ and every point $Q$ of $A$ over the resulting geometric point, $Q$ factors through `K.levK` if and only if $Q=x\cdot\big((m/\ell)\,P_{\bar{s}}\big)$ for some $x\in\Lambda$ lying in $L_0$.
--
--   This constructs a $\Gamma_0(\ell)$-type extra level structure on a fake elliptic curve out of a full level-$m$ structure, the subgroup being the line cut out by $L_0$ inside the $\ell$-torsion generated by $(m/\ell)P$. It is used in the fine and coarse moduli statements for the associated Shimura curves with extra level at $\ell$, and in the comparison of algebraic families with extra level to the analytic description.
